1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,032
My fingers never bleed, yet every single night this piano demands the exact same price in pure terror.

2
00:00:07,332 --> 00:00:13,836
The score on the music stand is entirely blank, but I hear every haunting note echo through the dark.

3
00:00:14,136 --> 00:00:21,096
Smoke curls lazily from the floorboards beneath the bench, smelling faintly of old ash and burning copper.

4
00:00:21,396 --> 00:00:27,468
I tried to stop playing once, but the room instantly grew so cold my breath turned to frost.

5
00:00:27,768 --> 00:00:34,008
The melody is a countdown, forcing my hands to move faster as the heat rises around the room.

6
00:00:34,308 --> 00:00:40,068
Every key I strike hammers a nail into a door that has already been locked from the outside.

7
00:00:40,368 --> 00:00:49,320
I finally recognize the haunting rhythm. It is not music at all. It is my own dying heartbeat.

8
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:57,012
The front door bursts into flames outside, proving the warning I refused to believe until it was too late.

9
00:00:57,312 --> 00:01:04,440
As the roof collapses, my fingers hit the final note, sealing the loop for tomorrow night's performance.

10
00:01:04,740 --> 00:01:12,708
Now the room is silent again. My fingers hover over the ivory keys, waiting for the very first note.
